# V - Ugur interatomic potential, switched, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * V_taper.ugur.ang V
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD: measured drift within noise for copper (0.002 meV/atom/ns against 176 for its hard twin).  BUT THIS RECORD IS NOT FIT FOR MD AT TEMPERATURE: it leaves bcc once the cell may change shape and its C' turns negative by 0.05 T_melt (see the MD lines below).  It pays for that on the dispersion: the switched sets average 12.8 % against the hard sets' 9.9 %, because switching the pair term off over the outer 15 % moves the force constants at the largest separations, which is the short-wavelength end, and nothing in the fit sees it
# MD: structure screened - holds its shape at 600 K (301 K, as equipartition requires).  This tested the SHAPE, not energy conservation; for that see the truncation line above.
# MD AT TEMPERATURE: DO NOT USE.  With the cell free to change shape (40 ps at 300 K, then a quench) the crystal leaves bcc: 0 % of the atoms keep it, 142 meV/atom below the static lattice (structure gate, lammps/gate/).  The 600 K screen holds the box shape fixed and cannot see this.
# MD AT TEMPERATURE: C' = (C11 - C12)/2 of the finite-temperature elastic constants turns negative by 0.05 T_melt (lammps/elastic_T.py): the crystal loses its shear stiffness when warm.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of V at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
